## Michael's Memo: New Season, New Opportunities

I'll be honest. This is one of my favorite times of year. The weather cools down, the leaves start to turn, and maybe best of all, football is back.

As a longtime football fan, I can't wait to see how this season unfolds: the energy, the rivalries, the underdog stories. There's just something about kickoff weekend that makes everything feel fresh and full of possibility.

Like football, business has its own kickoff moments. The start of a new client relationship. An advisor bringing in the right outside support. A business taking on a big growth opportunity. Those first plays matter. They set the tone for trust, momentum, and the chance to build something lasting.

At Serve Funding, that's how we see every introduction. It's not just about closing a deal. It's about starting strong, earning trust, and laying the foundation for long-term wins. And like football, it takes a team: entrepreneurs, advisors, bankers, and funding sources all working together to move the ball forward.

So as I settle in this weekend with a game on the screen, I'm reminded that what excites me most, on the field and in business, is that feeling of a fresh start, the kickoff of something that could turn into a great season.

Here's to kicking off more growth stories together.

Here to serve,

Michael Kodinsky, Founder & CEO

## Deal Highlight: $1MM Purchase-Order Facility for a Growing Coffee Trader

Like any good team driving down the field, sometimes a business needs the right play call to keep momentum going.

For a family-owned international green coffee trader, demand from corporate roasters surged almost overnight. The opportunity was there, but without additional working capital they risked stalling before the goal line. Their growth was outpacing their working capital. The firm had a facility advancing against purchase orders, but it was capped at $150,000 and that lender would not increase the line.

One of our asset-based lending partners introduced Serve Funding to the importer. Leveraging a nearly ten-year-old lender relationship, we secured a $1,000,000 purchase-order facility that let the client offset rising tariff costs through bulk-order discounts, pay overseas suppliers without delay, and keep production moving and customers happy.

The full story is in the case study: [$1MM PO Financing Line for a Coffee Trader](/blog/coffee-trader-po-financing).

{% callout type="tip" title="The right play at the right time" %}
This was more than a loan. It was capital that scaled with the business's growth and positioned it for long-term wins. At Serve Funding, we don't just fund businesses. We empower founders building thriving enterprises and lasting legacies.
{% /callout %}

